{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB07615 - MONDO_6004",
  "verbalization": "Tranilast is linked to Vasomotor Rhinitis through a series of indications that collectively suggest a potential mechanism of action. The evidence shows that Tranilast is associated with Allergic Rhinitis, which in turn is linked to several drugs—Isoflupredone Acetate, Ramatroban, and Mebhydrolin—all of which are indicated for Vasomotor Rhinitis. This suggests that Tranilast may exert a therapeutic effect through a shared pathway involving allergic inflammation, potentially modulating vascular tone or mast cell activation. The presence of multiple drugs with similar indications for Vasomotor Rhinitis implies that the condition may be influenced by a common mechanism, such as the inhibition of inflammatory mediators or the modulation of histamine release. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Tranilast in the management of Vasomotor Rhinitis through an indirect, inflammatory pathway.",
